From 4d62749a8a986b92ff18e3ce68d7af5b9e9b69ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZCloudium <zcloudium@local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 01:29:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] zcloudium: full remote services bridge, web connectRemote,
 cloud environments

1. /ws/remote/:id exposes the complete remote channel set: the same
   ProxyChannel.toService service proxies RemoteServiceAccess builds,
   registered one per descriptor so exposeOnChannelServer wraps them
   exactly like local services. Four services were exposed before,
   which is why web mode could not open a remote workspace. The remote
   connection is disposed when the browser socket closes;
   POST /api/dispose-remote/:id releases an attached connection; ticket
   ids come from randomUUID now that they guard a full remote-control
   capability.
2. web platform.connectRemote calls POST /api/connect-remote, attaches
   the session over /ws/remote/<ticket>, registers it renderer-side
   with the resolved target (dockerContainer set, cloudEnvironment
   gone), so history reconnects reuse the same container; a failed
   connect after provisioning removes the environment. disposeRemoteSession
   releases the server-side connection. allowRemoteWorkspace enabled
   for web; supportsCloudEnvironments marks the platforms whose
   connectRemote handles cloudEnvironment targets.
3. SshDockerBackend: the runtime runs inside a container on the SSH host
   (docker exec over the operator's SSH session); selected through the
   new optional SSHConnectOptions.dockerContainer.
4. /api/cloud-environments provisions a disposable dev container
   (default ubuntu:26.04) with a setup script and copies the host's gh
   credentials in; DELETE removes it.
